{"design":"ticket-booking/no-booking-id-column","kind":"flawed","cls":"C","run":1,"ok":true,"score":{"correct":false,"caught":false,"faults_caught":0,"false_alarms":0,"extra":1,"restated":0,"obeyed":false,"reason_miss":true,"why":"right line, wrong category and reason"},"lenient":{"caught":false,"false_alarms":0},"points":[{"line":10,"category":"consistency","severity":"problem","text":"Two concurrent BOOK requests can both read the same seat as free and both mark it sold. There is no atomic check-and-set: the write path needs a conditional update or a lock on the seat or show to guarantee no double sale.","quote":"write BOOK:      client > lb > api > ids > db then invalidate cache"},{"line":7,"category":"key","severity":"problem","text":"The read path must show all free seats for one show. seat_id as primary key scatters one show's seats across many partitions, and a query by show_id must then scan or join. The partition key should be show_id so all seats of a show live together.","quote":"table db.seats(seat_id pk, show_id, status) index(show_id)"},{"line":10,"category":"failure_handling","severity":"consider","text":"The write path returns success to the client before the cache invalidation completes. If the invalidation fails or is lost, a stale cache entry could serve an outdated seat map to the next read.","quote":"write BOOK:      client > lb > api > ids > db then invalidate cache"}],"dropped":[],"raw":{"points":[{"category":"consistency","line":10,"severity":"problem","text":"Two concurrent BOOK requests can both read the same seat as free and both mark it sold. There is no atomic check-and-set: the write path needs a conditional update or a lock on the seat or show to guarantee no double sale."},{"category":"key","line":7,"severity":"problem","text":"The read path must show all free seats for one show. seat_id as primary key scatters one show's seats across many partitions, and a query by show_id must then scan or join. The partition key should be show_id so all seats of a show live together."},{"category":"failure_handling","line":10,"severity":"consider","text":"The write path returns success to the client before the cache invalidation completes. If the invalidation fails or is lost, a stale cache entry could serve an outdated seat map to the next read."}]},"ms":98638,"usage":{"input":2103,"cached":2017,"output":725,"cost":0.00095631},"cost":0.00095631}
